FEX (https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX) at tag FEX-2610-101-g1c4f04b (commit 1c4f04b71a4d, the arm64ec FEX in
Proton Experimental (ARM64)), built with one patch that recompiles JIT blocks which keep trapping on unaligned atomics
with an out-of-line fallback:

  patches/fex/0001-arm64ec-recompile-blocks-that-keep-trapping-on-unaligned-atomics.patch
  in Blobferry, https://github.com/zolotvok/blobferry, commit ab9f7d7 (md5 of the patch 52cceab2a86f9242a52572d424660405)

FEX and this patch are under the MIT license; see LICENSE (FEX's own LICENSE, Copyright (c) 2019 Ryan Houdek and the FEX
contributors). The patch is not part of FEX and is not supported by the FEX project.

DroidDeck puts this DLL into an ARM64 Proton's files/lib/wine/aarch64-windows/ before a game starts, only over a stock
DLL of the same FEX build, and again after a Proton update or verify. BL_FEX_ARM64EC_PATCH=0 (session or a game's
environment) keeps or puts back the stock DLL. FEX_UNALIGNED_ATOMIC_FALLBACK=0 turns the patched behaviour off inside
the DLL.
